+# ECON-03b — Native market discovery and residential compost reclamation
+**Baseline:** ECON-03a ZIP, not an independent divergent application.
+**Files:** `include/galaxy/ResourceMarket.hpp`, `src/ResourceMarket.cpp`, `src/Simulation.cpp`, `src/colony_live_host.cpp`, `tests/ECON03bMarketRecoveryTests.cpp`, `tests/B70kLiveReclaimerTests.py`, `CMakeLists.txt`, design docs.
+
+The market module is deliberately read-only. It takes trusted outpost geography, validates real built sites, reads already-durable inventories and known resident needs, and builds nonmonetary geographic summaries/opportunities. It never posts a new item, authorizes an order or writes SQLite. Potential offers across sites are bounded against one site's aggregate potential surplus, but no inventory is reserved and multiple repeated scans must not be interpreted as multiple executable promises.
+
+The site-local powered reclaimer also transforms residential organic waste into local compost and residual sludge using a fixed 80/20 game recipe. Source balances remain local and included in existing persisted `ColonyLifeSupport` fields; existing wastewater/CO2 historical counters and snapshot formats remain intact. Distinct medical streams remain excluded. Storage-bound checks avoid invalid persisted quantities.
+
+The one-system colony host emits a four-resource `RESOURCE_MARKET` status line every 20 simulation ticks; relay's existing bounded allowlist transports the telemetry. This is not yet a visible market UI or a true cross-system execution engine.
+
+**Limits:** Only food, water and oxygen currently have first-class recurring NPC demand targets. No household consumption catalog, steam cycle, waste sorting plant, completed contract, cross-world trading, money, public player market or fully operational multi-region interstellar marketplace is claimed. Built production and factory delivery work remains separate.
